        {
          "id": 2026555185,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "No, it can be of any time standard. While PTP in general is based on TAI (UTC+37s) time standard, the alternate time scale offset TLV which can optionally be attached to the end of PTP announce messages is of custom time scale. The time scale which the sender is using like PST(Pacific Standard Time) is specified by the field displayName which follows immediately after timeofNextJump.",
          "author": {
            "id": 8237860,
            "username": "prastrip",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Prashant Tripathi",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
